{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgaUyt8D2uEyS8XjxeVZD","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I replaced the `sorry` in `Main.lean` with a proof, and `lean Main.lean` now runs with no errors or warnings.\n\nThe proof uses induction on the list:\n- **Empty list:** `myFilter p []` is `[]`, so the inequality is `0 ≤ 0`.\n- **List `x :: xs`:** I unfold `myFilter` and split on whether `p x` is true. If it is, the inequality becomes `ih` plus 1 on each side. If not, the filtered length is at most `xs.length`, which is less than `xs.length + 1`. `omega` closes both cases using the induction hypothesis `ih`.\n\n```lean\n  induction xs with\n  | nil => simp [myFilter]\n  | cons x xs ih =>\n    simp only [myFilter]\n    split\n    · simp only [List.length_cons]; omega\n    · simp only [List.length_cons]; omega\n```"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":7892,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"output_tokens":300,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"e3328706-2423-4873-a3a9-b96aa33ee8a9","uuid":"fb3a7a9e-1dfa-4bb3-a5eb-6c5643b9f9f1","timestamp":"2026-10-31T14:36:28.488Z","request_id":"req_011CgaUystZkij9BSbr8jnLc"}
